title: The Factory Councils Movement
subtitle: Elected councils in the workplaces are where Communist and Social Democratic workers meet.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: rf_mass
view-if: rf_councils_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; rf_councils_timer = 3

= The Factory Councils Movement

The factory councils elected under the 1920 law give Communists a foothold in plants where the unions are run by Social Democrats. Councils also run price-control committees as the mark collapses.

- @councils
- @unions
- @red_unions

@councils
title: Build a national congress of factory councils.
subtitle: Pleases the <span class="f-right">Right</span> and <span class="f-center">Middle Group</span>. Raises the revolutionary temperature.
on-arrival: {!
window.RF.lean(Q, {right: 2, center: 2});
Q.union_influence += 4;
Q.rev_situation += 3;
Q.spd_relation += 2;
!}

Factory council delegates from across the country meet under Communist leadership. The union leaders call it a rival organisation, but <span class="p-spd">SPD</span> members attend.

@unions
title: Work patiently inside the ADGB unions.
subtitle: Strong union influence. Pleases the <span class="f-right">Right</span>. Angers the <span class="f-ultra">Ultra-Left</span>.
on-arrival: {!
window.RF.lean(Q, {right: 3, ultra: -4});
Q.union_influence += 7;
Q.spd_relation += 3;
!}

Communists run for union posts and win some. The Ultra-Left complains that the party is serving the union bureaucracy instead of fighting it.

@red_unions
title: Leave the reformist unions and build red unions.
subtitle: Pleases the <span class="f-ultra">Ultra-Left</span>. Wrecks union influence. Moscow disapproves.
on-arrival: {!
window.RF.lean(Q, {ultra: 6, right: -5, center: -2});
Q.union_influence -= 12;
Q.spd_relation -= 6;
Q.moscow_trust -= 5;
!}

Militants tear up their union cards and found new revolutionary unions. They are pure, small, and cut off from millions of workers. The <span class="p-comintern">Comintern</span> has warned against exactly this.
